{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Shell|settings.define|Menu\\\\(|menu:|input.bind|input.label|Humanoid.pose|autoPause|live:' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -75; ls vendor/engine-repo/*LICENSE*\"","aggregated_output":"88:- 1184 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n278:- `input.bindButtons(root)` †: wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action\n279:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n293:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), wit [... omitted end of long line]\n304:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the ga [... omitted end of long line]\n459:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause [... omitted end of long line]\n469:- `new E.Game({ autoPause })`: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n493:- `game.menu(name, o)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, wa [... omitted end of long line]\n555:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n575:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its  [... omitted end of long line]\n637:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game,  [... omitted end of long line]\n679:- `E.Humanoid.pose(id, fn)` †: a held pose of the game's own: fn(J, w, rig) moves the joints (the rig's frame: forward, right, up) toward the pose by w, 0..1, which eases in and out as state.pose name [... omitted end of long line]\n680:- `E.Humanoid.poses` †: the held poses of a game's own, by id (the built-in poses are the rig's own solve: state.pose names either)\n693:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) at [... omitted end of long line]\n1155:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: ! [... omitted end of long line]\n1184:## 21d. Shell\n1186:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HT [... omitted end of long line]\n1187:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font: a family, titleFont), and scale: the whole interface that many times (a number, or a function of the window) f [... omitted end of long line]\n1188:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1189:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard [... omitted end of long line]\n1190:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1191:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1628:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1718:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\nvendor/engine-repo/LICENSE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
