ong line]\n35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p src/ui src/content; cat > docs/research.md <<'EOF'\n# Research ledger\n\nGame: Bomb Union. Source inspected 2026-11-06.\n\n## Verified primary-source facts\n- [Original manual](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/instructions/bombsquad.html): timed circuit work reveals a hidden one-to-three-digit code. Two cuts, removal, replacement/jumper, and two solder joints form the repair sequence. Each board uses a fixed shape or color replacement rule. Wrong work and fires have recovery windows. Frank instructs; Boris taunts. Evidence includes unlit cells; early submission is deliberate and consequential.\n- [Creator-maintained history](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/bombsquad.html): Intellivision/Intellivoice release, named designers and voice performers. Documents voice-priority and finished-component animation defects; this game keeps urgent instructions above taunts and settled parts stable.\n- [Original screenshot](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/images/bombsquad/BombSquadScreen.gif): inspected downloaded image; green PCB, cyan traces, bright component silhouettes and conspicuous timer.\n\n## Unknowns\nAn original music score is unconfirmed. Original voice hardware and physical controller/touch/TV playback are not available here. Universal cross-network WebRTC reachability is unknown.\n\n## Original additions\nBomb Union, municipal crew, partner Pip, saboteur Professor Quibble, all dialogue and case landmarks, authored campaign, evidence packs, recovery implementation, cooperative dispatch, procedural score/gibberish voices, native component/tool designs and editor are original.\n\n## Technical sources / actual revisions\n- Full my-3D2dge handoff v0.89.1, git 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691 (current main when fetched; matches PLAN reference). Read README, API, relevant API index, assets card, pointclick and adventure kits; adapt their native Game/Shell scene structure for fixed interaction.\n- AI Hub protocol 1 / session client 1.4.0, git 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869 (matches PLAN reference); official README/client/harness vendored byte-for-byte.\n- PeerJS 1.5.5 official guide/FAQ/release and vendored distribution; used only in standalone online flow.\n\nEngine changes are tracked separately in engine-changes.md. Third-party software is MIT licensed; notices retained under vendor and in the final HTML.\nEOF\ncat > docs/engine-changes.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes\n\nNone. The full native engine is vendored unchanged. Game-owned shapes, materials, rig poses, procedural instruments, Shell screens, settings and deterministic simulation extend public APIs.\nEOF\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Testing issue ledger\n\nEvery discovered defect receives an ID, severity, source check and resolution here. Hardware listening, real TV, physical touch/controller and cross-network NAT traversal remain unknown; emulation does not establish them.\n\n## Issues\n\n## Runs\nMachine-readable results live in evidence/verification.json and browser evidence files.\nEOF\ncat > package.json <<'EOF'\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"bomb-union\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\",\\\"private\\\":true,\\\"scripts\\\":{\\\"build\\\":\\\"node tools/build.mjs\\\",\\\"test\\\":\\\"node tools/verify.mjs\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"module\\\"}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p src/ui src/content; cat > docs/research.md <<'EOF'\n# Research ledger\n\nGame: Bomb Union. Source inspected 2026-11-06.\n\n## Verified primary-source facts\n- [Original manual](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/instructions/bombsquad.html): timed circuit work reveals a hidden one-to-three-digit code. Two cuts, removal, replacement/jumper, and two solder joints form the repair sequence. Each board uses a fixed shape or color replacement rule. Wrong work and fires have recovery windows. Frank instructs; Boris taunts. Evidence includes unlit cells; early submission is deliberate and consequential.\n- [Creator-maintained history](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/bombsquad.html): Intellivision/Intellivoice release, named designers and voice performers. Documents voice-priority and finished-component animation defects; this game keeps urgent instructions above taunts and settled parts stable.\n- [Original screenshot](https://history.blueskyrangers.com/mattelelectronics/games/images/bombsquad/BombSquadScreen.gif): inspected downloaded image; green PCB, cyan traces, bright component silhouettes and conspicuous timer.\n\n## Unknowns\nAn original music score is unconfirmed. Original voice hardware and physical controller/touch/TV playback are not available here. Universal cross-network WebRTC reachability is unknown.\n\n## Original additions\nBomb Union, municipal crew, partner Pip, saboteur Professor Quibble, all dialogue and case landmarks, authored campaign, evidence packs, recovery implementation, cooperative dispatch, procedural score/gibberish voices, native component/tool designs and editor are original.\n\n## Technical sources / actual revisions\n- Full my-3D2dge handoff v0.89.1, git 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691 (current main when fetched; matches PLAN reference). Read README, API, relevant API index, assets card, pointclick and adventure kits; adapt their native Game/Shell scene structure for fixed interaction.\n- AI Hub protocol 1 / session client 1.4.0, git 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869 (matches PLAN reference); official README/client/harness vendored byte-for-byte.\n- PeerJS 1.5.5 official guide/FAQ/release and vendored distribution; used only in standalone online flow.\n\nEngine changes are tracked separately in engine-changes.md. Third-party software is MIT licensed; notices retained under vendor and in the final HTML.\nEOF\ncat > docs/engine-changes.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes\n\nNone. The full native engine is vendored unchanged. Game-owned shapes, materials, rig poses, procedural instruments, Shell screens, settings and deterministic simulation extend public APIs.\nEOF\ncat > docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n# Testing issue ledger\n\nEvery discovered defect receives an ID, severity, source check and resolution here. Hardware listening, real TV, physical touch/controller and cross-network NAT traversal remain unknown; emulation does not establish them.\n\n## Issues\n\n## Runs\nMachine-readable results live in evidence/verification.json and browser evidence files.\nEOF\ncat > package.json <<'EOF'\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"bomb-union\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\",\\\"private\\\":true,\\\"scripts\\\":{\\\"build\\\":\\\"node tools/build.mjs\\\",\\\"test\\\":\\\"node tools/verify.mjs\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"module\\\"}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/ui/style.css <<'EOF'\n:root{color-scheme:dark;--mint:#9dffc6;--cream:#f4efd9;--orange:#ffb864}*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:#071319}body{font-family:'Trebuchet MS',system-ui,sans-serif}#screen{display:block;width:100vw;height:100vh;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}button,input,textarea{font:inherit}button{cursor:pointer}.esh{--ink:#f4efd9\"'!important;--accent:#a5ffca!important;--muted:#b2c5bd!important;--paper:#0c2229f2!important;--line:#54756c88!important;--title:'\"'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif\"'!important;--font:'\"'Trebuchet MS',system-ui,sans-serif\"'!important}.esh-sh{background:#04121bb8!important;padding-top:35px!important}.esh-ttl{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#05151bf5 0%,#05151bd9 36%,#05151b33 65%,#05151b00)!important}.esh-ttl>div{max-width:440px!important;padding-left:25px!important}.esh-ttl h1{text-transform:uppercase;font-size:67px!important;font-weight:900!important;letter-spacing:-.055em!important;line-height:.88!important;color:#f6f1d8;text-shadow:3px 3px #183d3a}.esh-ttl .esh-sub{font:normal 16px '\"'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;margin:16px 0 6px\"'!important;color:#9dffc6;letter-spacing:.08em}.esh-ttl .esh-k{margin-bottom:16px}.esh-ttl .esh-btns{max-width:280px}.esh-ttl .esh-tags{font-size:10px;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}.esh-mod{width:min(610px,96%)!important;border-radius:2px!important;padding:20px 24px!important;border-top:3px solid #a5ffca!important}.esh h2{font-size:29px!important;letter-spacing:-.035em}.esh-k{font-size:10px!important;font-weight:700}.esh .esh-m{font-size:13px!important}.esh button{border-radius:2px!important;min-height:40px!important;font-size:12px!important;letter-spacing:.03em!important}.esh button:hover,.esh button:focus{outline:2px solid #d2ffe1;outline-offset:2px;background:#234b48}.esh button.pri:hover{background:#d2ffe1}.esh-nav{opacity:.8}.esh-row{gap:10px}.esh-row small{font-size:10px!important}.esh input[type=range]{width:130px}.esh-toast{z-index:5;max-width:440px!important}.esh-toast.on{top:61px!important}.esh-btns{gap:6px!important;margin-top:14px!important}.esh-stats b{font-size:27px!important}.esh-sh[data-page=evidence] .esh-mod{width:min(770px,96%)!important}.esh-sh[data-page=credits] .esh-mod{width:min(700px,96%)!important}.esh-sh[data-page=editor] .esh-mod{width:min(750px,98%)!important}.bu-stencils{display:flex;gap:16px;justify-content:center;margin:15px 0}.bu-digit-block{text-align:center}.bu-digit-block small{display:block;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#b2c5bd;margin-top:5px}.bu-stencil{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:3px;width:65px;padding:5px;background:#06191e;border:1px solid #4c746b}.bu-cell{aspect-ratio:1;background:#32434a;position:relative;border:1px dotted #9ba9a766}.bu-cell.lit{background:#a3ffc2;border:1px solid #d7ffe7;box-shadow:0 0 5px #a3ffc255}.bu-cell.dark{background:#071116;border:1px solid #4a6d62}.bu-cell.dark:after{content:'\"'';position:absolute;left:25%;right:25%;top:45%;height:1px;background:#8ca99b}.bu-cell.unknown:after{content:'?';font:9px monospace;color:#8ba399;position:absolute;inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center}.bu-sectors{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:7px;margin-top:12px}.bu-sectors button{display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:9px\"'!important;gap:4px;min-height:62px!important}.bu-sectors button small{font-size:9px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0;color:#bdd3c8}.bu-sectors button.done{border-color:#9dffc6;background:#143e33}.bu-sectors button.hazard{border-color:#ff865e;color:#ffbd8e}.bu-help-glyphs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);gap:10px}.bu-help-glyphs .bu-stencil{width:53px}.bu-dials{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:15px;margin-top:15px}.bu-dial{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:8px}.bu-dial button{font-size:27px!important;text-align:ce