{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '2925,2955p' vendor/my-3d2dge.js; rg -n 'hook\\\\(|_ownRun\\\\(.input' vendor/my-3d2dge.js | head -14; rg -n 'hook\\\\(' vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -10; rg -n 'Audio|ART-|NET-|UI-' docs/testing.md\"","aggregated_output":"    if (!this._errKeys.has(key)) {\n      this._errKeys.add(key); this.errors.push({ where, scene: this.sceneName, message: msg, stack: e && e.stack });\n      console.error('my-3D2dge: error in ' + where + (this.sceneName ? ' (scene \"' + this.sceneName + '\")' : '') + ': ' + ((e && e.stack) || msg));\n    }\n    E.showError('error in ' + where + '()' + (this.sceneName && this.sceneName !== 'main' ? ' of scene \"' + this.sceneName + '\"' : ''), e);\n    if (this.onError) try { this.onError(e, where); } catch (e2) { /* ignore */ }\n  }\n  _step(dt) {\n    if (this._next) { const nx = this._next; this._next = null; this._enter(nx.name, nx.data); }\n    this.real += dt; this._shakeAmt *= Math.exp(-dt * 9); this.input.tick(dt); if (this._players) for (let i = 1; i < this._players.length; i++) this._players[i].tick(dt);   // (the other players: section 10j)\n    this.audio._tick(false);   // (the music clock: a song on game.real plays on through a pause)\n    for (const f of HOOKS.input) f(this, dt);\n    this._ownRun('input', dt);\n    if (this.input.padLost) { this._autoPause('controller'); if (this.shell) this.shell.toast('Controller disconnected', 'Press a button on a controller to use it, or play on.'); else this.note('CONTROLLER DISCONNECTED', 2.5); }\n    if (this.shell) this.shell._step();   // its screens move the focus with this step's input, and hold it back from the game\n    if (this._flash) this._flash.t += dt / Math.max(.05, this.timeScale);   // real time: slow motion does not stretch a flash\n    if (this._fade) { const out = this._fade.out; this._fadeStep(dt); if (out) return; }   // the old scene freezes while it fades out\n    const s = this.scene;\n    if (s && s.pausable && this.input.pressed('pause')) { this.paused = !this.paused; this.pauseReason = this.paused ? 'player' : null; this.audio.sfx('pause'); }\n    if (!this.paused) { this.pauseReason = null; this._goOn = false; }\n    this.audio._duck(this.paused);\n    // the player's zoom: the wheel, - and = and a pinch ask for it while a scene that allows it plays (input.zoom())\n    const I = this.input, zr = !this.paused && !(this.shell && this.shell.screen) && !!this.zoomRange();\n    I._zoomOn = zr; I._wheelOn = zr && (this._camera() || {}).wheel !== false;\n    if (this._zoomTo && !I._pinching && this._wall - this._zoomAt > .25) this._zoomApply();   // they stopped: the new zoom, drawn crisp\n    if (this.paused && !this.live && !this._goOn) return;   // (live: the world steps on under the menu)\n    if (!this.paused) { this._zoomFit(); const zk = I.zoom(); if (zk !== 1) this.zoomBy(zk); }\n    if (this.hitstop > 0) { this.hitstop -= dt; return; }\n    this.time += dt;\n    this.audio._tick(true);   // (a synced song: on game.time, it waits with the game)\n    const T = this._timers;\n2937:    this._ownRun('input', dt);\n4012:  if (!L) throw new Error('game.hook(\"' + kind + '\"): the hooks are input, step and enter');\n492:- `game.hook(kind, fn)` †: a function of the game's own on the engine's clock: kind 'input' fn(dt) every step, paused or not, after the input is read (a host's guard, an idle timer); 'step' fn(dt) eve [... omitted end of long line]\n18:| UI-001 | Critical, terminal flow | `tests/campaign-browser.py` ordinary-input training acceptance | After a successful deliberately confirmed code, the fallback screen guard returned to title and di [... omitted end of long line]\n27:| AUDIO-001 | Minor, persisted bus mismatch | Native settings/constructor integration review | Presentation construction reset existing effects and voice levels to 1 after settings had applied saved c [... omitted end of long line]\n28:| ART-001 | Medium, phone usability | Visual review of emulated iPhone portrait screenshot | Fixed 1.45-pixel native scale left the PCB only about 37% of phone width on a high-density portrait buffer. [... omitted end of long line]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read();needle=\\\"const view=()=>({screen:app.screen\\\";insert=\\\"let observedPause=false;\\\\ngame.hook('input',()=>{if(game.paused\"'!==observedPause){observedPause=game.paused;if(game.paused){cancelHold();if(!app.net?.online)app.audio.suspend(true);}else if(!(app.net?.mode==='\"'hub'&&app.net?.ended))app.audio.suspend(false);}});\\\\n\\\";s=s.replace(needle,insert+needle);open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode --check src/main.js\ncat >> docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Root UI integration review\n\n| ID | Severity | Found by | Defect and resolution | Regression |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| UI-002 | Medium, cooperative touch | Network/main contract review | Guest observation state was captured before the asynchronous board claim acknowledgment. It is now derived from current authority state every HUD update. | Exported two-player UI disposal and touch ownership checks |\n| UI-003 | Minor, failure caption | Simulation/main contract review | Timeout cause was checked as \"'`expired` instead of `time-expired`, showing the wrong failure title. Corrected the exact cause check. | Browser expiry/result cause check |\n| UI-004 | Minor, comfort setting | Native settings integration review | Custom view read a nonexistent reduceMotion setting instead of native game.reduceMotion. Custom camera/tool movement now uses the applied native property. | Art/audio reduced-motion checks |\n| UI-005 | Medium, urgent instruction | Simulation event/caption review | Wrong-cut fault and diagnosis events could be suppressed by a recent ordinary work-order caption. Fault, penalty and test events now receive urgent caption/voice priority. | Browser recovery and diagnostic playthrough |\n| UI-006 | Medium, live timer visibility | Overlay presentation review | Evidence and code menus hid the fuse while simulation continued. A single display-resolution fuse now remains visible over every active decision/menu screen and labels paused/live policy. | Browser overlay fuse visibility check |\n| UI-007 | Medium, held-tool lifecycle | Native pause source review | Escape/Options toggles native pause without calling game.pause(). A native input hook now observes pause transitions, cancels tool holds and synchronizes solo sound. | Browser pause-during-solder and resume check |\n\nRoot browser suite currently passes 43 checks, including actual mouse target actions, solder holds, native pause/settings, pad polling/focus and glyph change, code confirmation, developer tuning/reset, editor import/export/playtest, expiry, credits, real ten-second attract/wake, isolated saves, blocked/corrupted storage and phone/tablet touch emulation. Additional regression checks accompany final integration changes.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read();needle=\\\"const view=()=>({screen:app.screen\\\";insert=\\\"let observedPause=false;\\\\ngame.hook('input',()=>{if(game.paused\"'!==observedPause){observedPause=game.paused;if(game.paused){cancelHold();if(!app.net?.online)app.audio.suspend(true);}else if(!(app.net?.mode==='\"'hub'&&app.net?.ended))app.audio.suspend(false);}});\\\\n\\\";s=s.replace(needle,insert+needle);open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode --check src/main.js\ncat >> docs/testing.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Root UI integration review\n\n| ID | Severity | Found by | Defect and resolution | Regression |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| UI-002 | Medium, cooperative touch | Network/main contract review | Guest observation state was captured before the asynchronous board claim acknowledgment. It is now derived from current authority state every HUD update. | Exported two-player UI disposal and touch ownership checks |\n| UI-003 | Minor, failure caption | Simulation/main contract review | Timeout cause was checked as \"'`expired` instead of `time-expired`, showing the wrong failure title. Corrected the exact cause check. | Browser expiry/result cause check |\n| UI-004 | Minor, comfort setting | Native settings integration review | Custom view read a nonexistent reduceMotion setting instead of native game.reduceMotion. Custom camera/tool movement now uses the applied native property. | Art/audio reduced-motion checks |\n| UI-005 | Medium, urgent instruction | Simulation event/caption review | Wrong-cut fault and diagnosis events could be suppressed by a recent ordinary work-order caption. Fault, penalty and test events now receive urgent caption/voice priority. | Browser recovery and diagnostic playthrough |\n| UI-006 | Medium, live timer visibility | Overlay presentation review | Evidence and code menus hid the fuse while simulation continued. A single display-resolution fuse now remains visible over every active decision/menu screen and labels paused/live policy. | Browser overlay fuse visibility check |\n| UI-007 | Medium, held-tool lifecycle | Native pause source review | Escape/Options toggles native pause without calling game.pause(). A native input hook now observes pause transitions, cancels tool holds and synchronizes solo sound. | Browser pause-during-solder and resume check |\n\nRoot browser suite currently passes 43 checks, including actual mouse target actions, solder holds, native pause/settings, pad polling/focus and glyph change, code confirmation, developer tuning/reset, editor import/export/playtest, expiry, credits, real ten-second attract/wake, isolated saves, blocked/corrupted storage and phone/tablet touch emulation. Additional regression checks accompany final integration changes.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/browser.py';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace(\\\"page.keyboard.press('Escape');wait(page);before=state(page)['remaining'];\\\", \\\"aim(page,'C1:1');page.mouse.down();page.wait_for_timeout(90);page.keyboard.press('Escape');wait(page);page.mouse.up();wait(page);check('physical pause cancels a solder hold',state(page)['boards'][0]['hold'] is None);check('physical pause suspends procedural voice',snap(page)['audio']['paused']);before=state(page)['remaining'];\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"click(page,'Enter disarm code');check('code selection\\\", \\\"click(page,'Enter disarm code');check('decision overlays retain readable fuse',page.locator('#bu-global-fuse').is_visible());check('code selection\\\")\n# Full regression must remain finite even a failed gameplay action.\ns=s.replace(\\\"page=context.new_page();errors=[]\\\", \\\"page=context.new_page();page.set_default_timeout(10000);errors=[]\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/verify.mjs browser audio\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '3045,3086p' vendor/my-3d2dge.js; cat docs/testing.md | tail -38; command -v biome; command -v ruff; ls -lh ../*.html; ls -la vendor/hub-repo | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '3045,3086p' vendor/my-3d2dge.js; cat docs/testing.md | tail -38; command -v biome; command -v ruff; ls -lh ../*.html; ls -la vendor/hub-repo | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"const STANDARD_SETTINGS = {\n  fullscreen: { group: 'Display', label: 'Full screen', type: 'fullscreen', value: null },   // the player's choice: true, false (turned it off), null (never chose)\n  zoom: { group: 'Display', label: 'Camera zoom', type: 'slider', value: 1, min: ZOOM_PLAYER[0], max: ZOOM_PLAYER[1], step: .05, unit: '×', help: 'Closer or farther than the game frames it. In play: the mouse wheel, - and =, or a pinch', apply: g => g._zoomApply(false, true) },\n  frameRate: { group: 'Display', label: 'Frame rate', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['60', '60'], ['full', 'Full']], help: 'Auto: every refresh while the game keeps up, every other one, evenly, when it can\\'t. 60: every other refresh on a 120 Hz screen. Full: every refresh' },\n  showFps: { group: 'Display', label: 'Show frame rate', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'At the top of the screen: frames drawn a second, the screen\\'s refresh and a frame\\'s cost' },\n  scale: { group: 'Display', label: 'Pixel scaling', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['sharp', 'Sharp'], ['fill', 'Fill']], help: 'Sharp: every pixel the same size. Fill: the whole screen', apply: (g, v) => g.screen.setScale(v) },\n  filter: { group: 'Display', label: 'Screen filter', type: 'select', value: 'clean', options: [['clean', 'Clean'], ['scanlines', 'Scanlines'], ['crt', 'CRT']], help: 'Scanlines: the dark lines between a TV\\'s rows. CRT: those, its colored stripes and its darker corners', apply: (g, v) => { g.screen.filter = v; } },\n  sound: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound', type: 'toggle', value: true, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.mute(!v) },\n  volume: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Volume', type: 'slider', value: .7, apply: (g, v) => g.audio.setVolume(v) },\n  music: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Music', type: 'slider', value: .5, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.musicVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\n  effects: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Effects', type: 'slider', value: 1, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.sfxVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\n  background: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Sound in the background', type: 'toggle', value: false, help: 'Keep playing sound while the page is hidden' },\n  audioOffset: { group: 'Sound', label: 'Audio offset', type: 'slider', value: 0, min: -100, max: 300, step: 5, unit: ' ms', calibrate: true, help: 'The music this much earlier, for speakers or headphones that lag (wireless ones: 150 to 250). Calibrate: tap on the clicks you hear', apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.offset = v / 1000; } },\n  motion: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Reduce motion', type: 'toggle', value: g => !!g.reduceMotion, help: 'No screen shake, shorter flashes, still menus', apply: (g, v) => { g.reduceMotion = !!v; } },\n  shake: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen shake', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\n  flashes: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen flashes', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\n  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\n  deadzone: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Stick dead zone', type: 'slider', value: .18, min: .05, max: .5, step: .01, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.deadzone = v; } },\n  invertY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert aim up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertAimY = !!v; } },\n  invertMoveX: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move left and right', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveX = !!v; } },\n  invertMoveY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert move up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.invertMoveY = !!v; } },\n  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.glyphs = v; } },\n  rumble: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Vibration', type: 'slider', value: .6, apply: (g, v) => { for (const q of g._players || [g.input]) q.rumbleScale = v; } },\n  touch: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Touch buttons', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Automatic'], ['on', 'Always'], ['off', 'Hidden']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\n  hand: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Buttons on', type: 'select', value: 'right', options: [['right', 'Right'], ['left', 'Left']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\n  touchSize: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button size', type: 'slider', value: 62, min: 44, max: 88, step: 2, unit: ' px', apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\n  touchOpacity: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Button opacity', type: 'slider', value: .8, min: .3, max: 1, step: .05, apply: g => g.input._touchSync() }\n};\n/** a value for a setting, checked: the value kept, or undefined when it can't be one */\nfunction settingValue(sp, v) {\n  if (sp.type === 'toggle') return typeof v === 'boolean' ? v : undefined;\n  if (sp.type === 'fullscreen') return v === true || v === false || v === null ? v : undefined;\n  if (sp.type === 'slider') return typeof v === 'number' && isFinite(v) ? clamp(v, sp.min === undefined ? 0 : sp.min, sp.max === undefined ? 1 : sp.max) : undefined;\n  if (sp.type === 'select') return (sp.options || []).some(o => (Array.isArray(o) ? o[0] : o) === v) ? v : undefined;\n  if (sp.type === 'bindings') {\n    if (!v || typeof v !== 'object' || Array.isArray(v)) return undefined;\n    const out = {};\n    for (const a in v) { const b = v[a]; if (!b || typeof b !== 'object') continue; const o = {}; for (const k of ['keys', 'pad']) if (Array.isArray(b[k])) o[k] = b[k].filter(c => typeof c === 'string' && BINDABLE.test(c) && padCode(c) === (k === 'pad')).slice(0, 4); out[a] = o; }\n    return out;\n  }\n  return v === undefined || typeof v === 'function' ? undefined : v;   // a type of the game's own: any JSON value\n}\n\n## Runs\nMachine-readable results live in evidence/verification.json and browser evidence files.\n\n### Simulation and integration audit\n\n| ID | Severity | Found by | Defect and resolution | Regression |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SIM-001 | Minor | State-machine branch review followed by focused stock regression | Securing a board while holding an extra spare cleared the held ID without returning that spare. Completion now safely returns it to available stock. | `Held stock remains safe at board completion` |\n| SIM-002 | Medium, developer flow only | Fault-injection branch review followed by focused recovery regression | Developer-injected fire on an already secure board could not receive an extinguisher command because completion blocked all tools. Completed-board fire now permits begin/end extinguisher actions and never republishes evidence. | `Developer fire cannot strand an already secured board` |\n| SIM-003 | Medium, cooperative UI | Main/simulation contract audit | Vote UI tracks proposal IDs, but proposals initially lacked stable IDs, suppressing later vote panels. Every proposal now has a stable unique ID; the app must also reset its local seen-ID on case start. | `Voting rules, veto, majority and departure` checks repeated proposal IDs |\n\n| UI-001 | Critical, terminal flow | `tests/campaign-browser.py` ordinary-input training acceptance | After a successful deliberately confirmed code, the fallback screen guard returned to title and discarded the resolved state before showing results. The root app now routes any terminal state to results before the title fallback. | Ordinary campaign training-to-results smoke and full campaign acceptance |\n\nSimulation test evidence: `tests/simulation.mjs` exports `runSimulationTests()` for the single verification command. It presently reports 1,742 passing assertions, including full ordinary-command campaign completion, all party sizes, truthful dark evidence, wrong cuts/spares, heat/fire, stock, ownership, duplicates, stale revisions, bounded holds, voting, simultaneous expiry, editor import/export, live tuning, and deterministic seed fidelity. These are headless model checks; they do not establish browser input, rendered visibility, or listening quality.\n\n\n### Presentation integration audit\n\n| ID | Severity | Found by | Defect and resolution | Regression |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| AUDIO-001 | Minor, persisted bus mismatch | Native settings/constructor integration review | Presentation construction reset existing effects and voice levels to 1 after settings had applied saved choices and the authored 0.75 voice default. Constructor now preserves settings-applied levels, including zero, so reloads agree with the real graph. | `Audio construction preserves persisted effects and voice mute`; `Reload preserves saved independent voice mute and effects` in `tests/art-headless.mjs` |\n| ART-001 | Medium, phone usability | Visual review of emulated iPhone portrait screenshot | Fixed 1.45-pixel native scale left the PCB only about 37% of phone width on a high-density portrait buffer. Portrait framing now sizes the native board to 90% of buffer width, centers it above the instruction strip, and scales focus hit regions with the projected artwork. | `Phone portrait PCB occupies ninety percent of buffer width`; `Phone portrait workspace stays between fuse and order strip`; `Enlarged portrait terminals remain reachable and inside workspace` |\n\nCampaign browser acceptance completed with 508 checks and 273 player-facing UI actions, zero failures. A fresh desktop page navigated title, training, all three authored cases, inferred code confirmation, final ending/results, and acknowledgments. It repaired every board using ordinary pointer/keyboard controls, performed a deliberate wrong-cut recovery and wrong replacement recovery, tested actual spare diagnostics, and extinguished the controlled relay fire. No developer state writes, invulnerability, hidden-code reads, or direct gameplay method calls were used. Work, evidence and result screenshots from all four beats are in `evidence/campaign-*.png`; counts/actions are in `evidence/campaign-browser.json`. First-time human pacing remains unknown.\n\n### Root UI integration review\n\n| ID | Severity | Found by | Defect and resolution | Regression |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| UI-002 | Medium, cooperative touch | Network/main contract review | Guest observation state was captured before the asynchronous board claim acknowledgment. It is now derived from current authority state every HUD update. | Exported two-player UI disposal and touch ownership checks |\n| UI-003 | Minor, failure caption | Simulation/main contract review | Timeout cause was checked as `expired` instead of `time-expired`, showing the wrong failure title. Corrected the exact cause check. | Browser expiry/result cause check |\n| UI-004 | Minor, comfort setting | Native settings integration review | Custom view read a nonexistent reduceMotion setting instead of native game.reduceMotion. Custom camera/tool movement now uses the applied native property. | Art/audio reduced-motion checks |\n| UI-005 | Medium, urgent instruction | Simulation event/caption review | Wrong-cut fault and diagnosis events could be suppressed by a recent ordinary work-order caption. Fault, penalty and test events now receive urgent caption/voice priority. | Browser recovery and diagnostic playthrough |\n| UI-006 | Medium, live timer visibility | Overlay presentation review | Evidence and code menus hid the fuse while simulation continued. A single display-resolution fuse now remains visible over every active decision/menu screen and labels paused/live policy. | Browser overlay fuse visibility check |\n| UI-007 | Medium, held-tool lifecycle | Native pause source review | Escape/Options toggles native pause without calling game.pause(). A native input hook now observes pause transitions, cancels tool holds and synchronizes solo sound. | Browser pause-during-solder and resume check |\n\nRoot browser suite currently passes 43 checks, including actual mouse target actions, solder holds, native pause/settings, pad polling/focus and glyph change, code confirmation, developer tuning/reset, editor import/export/playtest, expiry, credits, real ten-second attract/wake, isolated saves, blocked/corrupted storage and phone/tablet touch emulation. Additional regression checks accompany final integration changes.\n/home/micha/.local/bin/biome\n/home/micha/.local/bin/ruff\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1.5M Nov  6 05:10 ../Bomb-Union-Bomb-Squad-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-045026.html\ntotal 348\ndrwxr-xr-x   15 micha micha   4096 Nov  6 04:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 micha micha   4096 Nov  6 04:52 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x    7 micha micha   4096 Nov  6 04:52 .git\n-rw-r--r--    1 micha micha    477 Nov  6 04:52 .gitattributes\n-rw-r--r--    1 micha micha    345 Nov  6 04:52 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--    1 micha micha   2783 Nov  6 04:52 CLAUDE.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 micha micha   1027 Nov  6 04:52 HANDOFF.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace(\\\"{key:'candidates',label:\\\",\\\"{key:'textScale',label:'Text size',type:'slider',value:1,min:.85,max:1.25,step:.05,group:'Comfort',apply:(g,v)=>{document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--bu-text',v);if(g.shell?.root)window.dispatchEvent(new Event('resize'));}},{key:'candidates',label:\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"Math.min(2.12,innerWidth/930))\\\", \\\"Math.min(2.12,innerWidth/930))*(game.settings.textScale||1)\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"page=(page+groups.length)%groups.length;const [name,items]=groups[page];\\\", \\\"const pages=groups.flatMap(([name,items])=>{const size=name==='Source Information'?4:name==='Engine Feedback'||name==='Credits & licenses'?3:4;return Array.from({length:Math.ceil(items.length/size)},(_,i)=>[name+(items.length>size?' · '+(i+1):''),items.slice(i*size,i*size+size)]);});page=(page+pages.length)%pages.length;const [name,items]=pages[page];\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"\"'${page+1} / ${groups.length}\",\"${page+1} / ${pages.length}\")\nopen(p,'\"'w').write(s)\np='tests/browser.py';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"click(page,'Next page');check('credits required feedback pagination','Testing Feedback' in page.locator('body').inner_text());\\\", \\\"\\\\n  for _ in range(5):\\\\n   if 'Testing Feedback' in page.locator('body').inner_text():break\\\\n   click(page,'Next page')\\\\n  check('credits required feedback pagination','Testing Feedback' in page.locator('body').inner_text());\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> src/ui/style.css <<'EOF'\n#bu-hud{font-size:calc(clamp(15px,1.5vw,29px) * var(--bu-text,1))}#bu-global-fuse{font-size:calc(clamp(15px,1.5vw,29px) * var(--bu-text,1))}\nEOF\nnode --check src/main.js\nls vendor/hub\nnode --check tools/verify.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
