{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\| (SIM-|NET-|UI-|AUDIO-|ART-|TOUCH-)' docs/testing.md; sed -n '10,75p' tools/build.mjs; sed -n '95,160p' tools/verify.mjs; ls -la ../\"","aggregated_output":"14:| SIM-001 | Minor | State-machine branch review followed by focused stock regression | Securing a board while holding an extra spare cleared the held ID without returning that spare. Completion now sa [... omitted end of long line]\n15:| SIM-002 | Medium, developer flow only | Fault-injection branch review followed by focused recovery regression | Developer-injected fire on an already secure board could not receive an extinguisher c [... omitted end of long line]\n16:| SIM-003 | Medium, cooperative UI | Main/simulation contract audit | Vote UI tracks proposal IDs, but proposals initially lacked stable IDs, suppressing later vote panels. Every proposal now has a st [... omitted end of long line]\n18:| UI-001 | Critical, terminal flow | `tests/campaign-browser.py` ordinary-input training acceptance | After a successful deliberately confirmed code, the fallback screen guard returned to title and di [... omitted end of long line]\n27:| AUDIO-001 | Minor, persisted bus mismatch | Native settings/constructor integration review | Presentation construction reset existing effects and voice levels to 1 after settings had applied saved c [... omitted end of long line]\n28:| ART-001 | Medium, phone usability | Visual review of emulated iPhone portrait screenshot | Fixed 1.45-pixel native scale left the PCB only about 37% of phone width on a high-density portrait buffer. [... omitted end of long line]\n36:| UI-002 | Medium, cooperative touch | Network/main contract review | Guest observation state was captured before the asynchronous board claim acknowledgment. It is now derived from current authority  [... omitted end of long line]\n37:| UI-003 | Minor, failure caption | Simulation/main contract review | Timeout cause was checked as `expired` instead of `time-expired`, showing the wrong failure title. Corrected the exact cause check [... omitted end of long line]\n38:| UI-004 | Minor, comfort setting | Native settings integration review | Custom view read a nonexistent reduceMotion setting instead of native game.reduceMotion. Custom camera/tool movement now uses t [... omitted end of long line]\n39:| UI-005 | Medium, urgent instruction | Simulation event/caption review | Wrong-cut fault and diagnosis events could be suppressed by a recent ordinary work-order caption. Fault, penalty and test even [... omitted end of long line]\n40:| UI-006 | Medium, live timer visibility | Overlay presentation review | Evidence and code menus hid the fuse while simulation continued. A single display-resolution fuse now remains visible over ever [... omitted end of long line]\n41:| UI-007 | Medium, held-tool lifecycle | Native pause source review | Escape/Options toggles native pause without calling game.pause(). A native input hook now observes pause transitions, cancels tool [... omitted end of long line]\n49:| TOUCH-001 | Medium, touch target reachability | Real touchscreen-tap training driver in phone emulation | A contextual action beside the left lead covered the next right lead, so a direct tap could  [... omitted end of long line]\n50:| TOUCH-002 | Medium, contextual solder assistance | Real touchscreen-tap contextual hold probe | Global pointer-up ended an assisted solder hold before its safe threshold. Assisted holds now survive  [... omitted end of long line]\n56:| NET-001 | Medium, seeded cooperative replay | Adapter lifecycle review followed by a focused network replay regression | Guest start detection used only case ID and seed, so retrying the identical d [... omitted end of long line]\n57:| NET-002 | Critical, Hub terminal lifecycle | Exact final-state comparison against the exported HTML after official harness time-up | After the fuse expired, the short final-snapshot delivery interva [... omitted end of long line]\nconst read = (p) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, p), \"utf8\");\nconst escapeScript = (s) => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, \"<\\\\/script\");\nconst hub = read(\"vendor/hub/session.js\");\nconst scripts = [\n\t\"vendor/my-3d2dge.js\",\n\t\"vendor/peerjs.min.js\",\n\t\"src/sim/content.js\",\n\t\"src/sim/model.js\",\n\t\"src/net/network.js\",\n\t\"src/view/art.js\",\n\t\"src/audio/audio.js\",\n\t\"src/main.js\",\n];\nconst reportPath = path.resolve(root, \"../exit-interview.json\");\nconst report = fs.existsSync(reportPath)\n\t? fs.readFileSync(reportPath, \"utf8\")\n\t: JSON.stringify({\n\t\t\tsourceInformation: {\n\t\t\t\tsource: \"Bomb Squad (1982)\",\n\t\t\t\tplan: \"PLAN.md\",\n\t\t\t\tusage: \"added on import\",\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t\ttestingFeedback: [\"unknown\"],\n\t\t\tengineFeedback: [\"unknown\"],\n\t\t\tpromptFeedback: [\"unknown\"],\n\t\t});\nconst metadata =\n\t'<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=1,user-scalable=no,viewport-fit=cover\"><meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Repair sectors, deduce the shared stencil code and disarm the device together.\"><meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"D-pad/left stick move focus; Cross apply or hold; Circle back/drop; L1/R1 tools; Square test; Triangle repeat; R2 evidence; Options menu.\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">';\nlet html = `<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><script>${hub}</script>\\n${metadata}<title>Bomb Union — Small repairs. Enormous consequences.</title><style id=\"bu-style\">${read(\"src/ui/style.css\")}</style></head><body><canvas id=\"screen\" aria-label=\"Bomb Union native circuit workspace\"></canvas><div id=\"bu-loading\" class=\"bu-loading\">BOMB UNION · Checking continuity…</div>\\n`;\nhtml += `<script>globalThis.BU=globalThis.BU||{};BU.REPORT=${escapeScript(report)};</script>\\n`;\nfor (const source of scripts)\n\thtml += `<script>\\n${escapeScript(read(source))}\\n</script>\\n`;\nconst notices = [\n\t\"vendor/ENGINE-LICENSE\",\n\t\"vendor/PEERJS-LICENSE\",\n\t\"vendor/hub/LICENSE\",\n]\n\t.filter((p) => fs.existsSync(path.join(root, p)))\n\t.map((p) => `${p}\\n${read(p)}`)\n\t.join(\"\\n\\n\");\nhtml += `<!-- Third-party notices\\n${notices.replace(/-->/g, \"-- >\")}\\n-->\\n</body></html>\\n`;\nconst output = path.resolve(root, `../${project.slug}.html`);\nfs.writeFileSync(output, html);\nfs.writeFileSync(\n\tpath.join(root, \"evidence/build.json\"),\n\tJSON.stringify(\n\t\t{\n\t\t\ttitle: project.title,\n\t\t\toutput: path.basename(output),\n\t\t\tbytes: Buffer.byteLength(html),\n\t\t\tsha256: crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(html).digest(\"hex\"),\n\t\t\thubSha256: crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(hub).digest(\"hex\"),\n\t\t\tengineRevision: \"8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691\",\n\t\t\thubRevision: \"35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869\",\n\t\t\tengineVersion: \"0.89.1\",\n\t\t\tclientVersion: \"1.4.0\",\n\t\t\tpeerVersion: \"1.5.5\",\n\t\t},\n\t\tnull,\n\t\t2,\n\t),\n);\nconsole.log(`Built ${path.basename(output)}`);\n\t\t\"hub:session-minutes\",\n\t])\n\t\tcheck(html.includes(`name=\"${field}\"`), `metadata ${field}`);\n\ttry {\n\t\tconst r = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"../exit-interview.json\", \"utf8\"));\n\t\tcheck(\n\t\t\tObject.keys(r).sort().join(\",\") ===\n\t\t\t\t\"aiHub,engineFeedback,promptFeedback,sourceInformation,testingFeedback\",\n\t\t\t\"report object shape\",\n\t\t);\n\t\tcheck(r.sourceInformation.usage === \"added on import\", \"usage exact\");\n\t\tcheck(\n\t\t\tr.testingFeedback.length === 4 &&\n\t\t\t\tr.engineFeedback.length === 6 &&\n\t\t\t\tr.promptFeedback.length === 4,\n\t\t\t\"feedback question counts\",\n\t\t);\n\t\tcheck(\n\t\t\tObject.values(r.sourceInformation).every(\n\t\t\t\t(x) => typeof x === \"string\" && x.length,\n\t\t\t),\n\t\t\t\"complete source info\",\n\t\t);\n\t\tcheck(\n\t\t\tr.aiHub.name === \"Bomb Union\" &&\n\t\t\t\tr.aiHub.genre === \"Puzzle\" &&\n\t\t\t\tr.aiHub.players === \"1–4\",\n\t\t\t\"catalogue values\",\n\t\t);\n\t\tcheck(\n\t\t\thtml.includes(JSON.stringify(r)) ||\n\t\t\t\thtml.includes(fs.readFileSync(\"../exit-interview.json\", \"utf8\")),\n\t\t\t\"credits and report source consistency\",\n\t\t);\n\t} catch (e) {\n\t\tcheck(false, \"exit interview\", e.message);\n\t}\n}\nfs.writeFileSync(\n\t\"evidence/verification.json\",\n\tJSON.stringify(\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tchecks,\n\t\t\tfailures,\n\t\t\tgroups: all ? [\"all\"] : [...groups],\n\t\t\tresults: evidence,\n\t\t},\n\t\tnull,\n\t\t2,\n\t),\n);\nfor (const f of failures) console.log(`FAIL ${f}`);\nconsole.log(`${checks} checks, ${failures.length} failures`);\nif (failures.length) process.exitCode = 1;\ntotal 1636\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  6 05:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha    4096 Nov  6 04:50 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 9 micha micha    4096 Nov  6 05:13 Bomb-Union-Bomb-Squad-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-045026\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1589521 Nov  6 05:15 Bomb-Union-Bomb-Squad-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-045026.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   49007 Nov  6 04:50 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    2294 Nov  6 05:03 PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   12500 Nov  6 04:50 TASK.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
