{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nr={\n'sourceInformation':{\n'date':'2026-11-06 04:50:26',\n'source':'Bomb Squad (1982, Intellivision / Mattel Electronics)',\n'plan':'PLAN.md',\n'genre':'Real-time puzzle / light simulation',\n'perspective':'Fixed native 2.5D city dioramas and an almost-overhead orthographic circuit workspace',\n 'tech':'JavaScript, HTML and CSS; full my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691); AI Hub protocol 1 / client 1.4.0; PeerJS 1.5.5; Web Audio',\n'artDirection':'Original native pixel art: substantial green PCBs, cyan traces, bright patterned components, metallic tools, warm/cool municipal city dioramas and response crew',\n'animation':'Native Humanoid rigs and poses, native game tweens, state-driven tool contact/settle, diagnostic pulses, foam, sparks and city outcome reactions',\n'audio':'Original code-synthesized electronic music, tool/city effects and distinct formant-like gibberish voices; actual music bus defaults to 10%; no audio files; listening quality unknown',\n'online':'1–4 cooperative technicians sharing one authoritative device, claims, evidence and code votes; official Hub shared-world lifecycle and real standalone PeerJS Cloud/WebRTC host/join/reconnect. Same-computer two-page connectivity verified; cross-network NAT reachability unknown',\n'testing':'Headless deterministic simulation/native draw tests and Chromium 153 with Playwright 1.63; ordinary-control full campaign, standard gamepad and touch emulation, offline audio, two-page WebRTC, official Hub normal/lag/loss/host-leave/server scenarios. Physical controller, touch, TV and listening checks unknown',\n'research':'Read original Blue Sky Rangers manual and creator history, inspected original circuit screenshot, current full engine documentation and pointclick/adventure examples, official Hub README/client/harness and PeerJS documentation; research ledger included',\n'environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux / Ubuntu on WSL2',\n'model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra',\n'usage':'added on import'\n},\n'testingFeedback':[\n'16 issues found by automated tests and integration reviews; all fixed and recorded with regressions in docs/testing.md.',\n'2 critical/game-breaking issues: successful disposal discarded results, and a Hub terminal-state restart. Both fixed.',\n'The ordinary-control full campaign playthrough: fresh training through all three disposals, recovery, diagnosis, fire and credits, with no developer state writes.',\n'The initial title-only smoke check had the least gameplay coverage; it was useful mainly for loading and visual composition.'\n],\n'engineFeedback':[\n'Native shaded pixel assets, Humanoid rigs and the controller Shell work together in one renderer.',\n'I initially assumed physical pause always called game.pause(), and underestimated buffer-versus-CSS scaling on dense phones; source inspection and regression checks corrected both.',\n'The authoritative deterministic repair/evidence simulation, seeded content validator and cooperative transport adapters.',\n'Coordinating native fixed steps and menus with online wall-clock authority, cancelable holds and audiovisual lifecycle.',\n'None. The engine is unmodified; game-owned shapes, materials, poses, instruments, settings, screens and input hooks extend its existing APIs.',\n'A single documented pause/lifecycle notification covering physical buttons, menu calls, blur and controller loss would simplify integration.'\n],\n'promptFeedback':[\n'The primary-source references and concrete completion gates kept the repair, deduction and verification goals clear.',\n'TASK owns naming while PLAN describes a full campaign and a shorter Hub dispatch; those required separate explicit configurations.',\n'Keeping touch-assisted holds, native pause, cooperative authority and stencil deduction consistent through the same repair rules.',\n'Add a compact machine-readable acceptance schema and fixed module contracts beside the prose; retain the explicit unavailable-hardware boundaries.'\n],\n'aiHub':{\n'name':'Bomb Union',\n'tagline':'Small repairs. Enormous consequences.',\n'description':'Clock in with a municipal bomb-disposal crew, repair hazardous circuits and read the stencil evidence they reveal. Work solo or share sectors with up to four technicians, then deliberately commit to the disarm code.',\n'type':'Game',\n'genre':'Puzzle',\n'source':'Bomb Squad (1982)',\n'series':'',\n'players':'1–4',\n'controls':'D-pad/WASD/mouse/tap targets; Cross/Space apply; L1/R1 or 1–4 tools; Square/E test; Triangle/R repeat; R2/Tab evidence; Options/Escape menu.',\n'tags':['co-op','pixel art','retro','comedy','top-down','puzzle']\n}}\np=pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json');p.write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n');assert json.loads(p.read_text())==r\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tools/verify.mjs package\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
